cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use bux in your research, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "bux: architecture and data ablations in a few lines"
abstract: >-
  bux is a JAX framework for comparing language models. A model is an algebra over
  the residual stream, written in a short .bux file that also says how to train it,
  and any line of the file becomes a sweep.
authors:
  - family-names: Pavlichenko
    given-names: Nikita
repository-code: https://github.com/pilot7747/bux
url: https://bux.readthedocs.io
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - jax
  - flax
  - language models
  - ablations
  - deep learning
